                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">Production of Mischmetal from bastnaesite by wet chemical attack and fused salt electrolysis. The product contains 53% Ce, 21% La, 17% Nd, 6% Pr, 0.2% Sm, the rest consistin of Eu, Gd and others. The overall quality of the data is poor. It however may be used as alloying constituent in HSLA steels, nodular iron and hydrogen storage in metal hydride batteries (LaNi5).This dataset is not to be used when mischmetal is a substantial part of the system modelled ;
CAS number: 008049-20-5; 
Synonyms: cerium mischmetal, rare earth mischmetal, misch metal; 
UUID: b5cd8fc8-fb6e-3a58-b36d-7a2a6bf90773</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
